\section{Conditions}{

The errors of the credential, argument, cache and metadata layers carry a
class, so that a script can handle one kind and let the others through,
for example \code{tryCatch(jatos_connection(), jatosr_no_token = function(cnd) NULL)}. Errors from the server keep the \code{httr2} classes (\code{httr2_http_401}
and so on); a file that is not valid JSON, a file that could not be
written and a request that never reached the server are plain errors.
\itemize{
\item \code{jatosr_bad_argument}: an argument of the wrong type, length or value,
from any function.
\item \code{jatosr_bad_profile}: a profile name that is not an identifier.
\item \code{jatosr_no_host}: no host for the profile, from \code{\link[=jatos_connection]{jatos_connection()}} and
\code{\link[=jatos_study_links]{jatos_study_links()}}.
\item \code{jatosr_no_token}: no token for the profile anywhere, or a cancelled
prompt, from \code{\link[=jatos_connection]{jatos_connection()}}.
\item \code{jatosr_keyring_unreadable}: the credential store holds the profile's
entry but cannot be read (locked, or a broken backend).
\item \code{jatosr_keyring_write_failed}: the credential store refused the token,
from \code{\link[=jatos_set_credentials]{jatos_set_credentials()}}; the profile configuration is put back
as it was.
\item \code{jatosr_no_store}: no persistent credential store on this system, from
\code{\link[=jatos_set_credentials]{jatos_set_credentials()}}.
\item \code{jatosr_needs_interactive}: a prompt is needed and the session cannot
show one, from \code{\link[=jatos_set_credentials]{jatos_set_credentials()}} without a \code{token} and
\code{\link[=jatos_remove_credentials]{jatos_remove_credentials()}} with \code{confirm = TRUE}.
\item \code{jatosr_config_write_failed}: the profile configuration file could not
be written; nothing was stored.
\item \code{jatosr_bad_metadata}: not a metadata tibble, or one lacking columns or
ids; a \code{metadata.json} that cannot be imported.
\item \code{jatosr_cache_layout}: a directory that is not a cache written by
jatosr, or a cache without a \code{metadata.json}.
\item \code{jatosr_zip_unreadable}: an answer or a file that is not a zip, or one
that cannot be unpacked.
\item \code{jatosr_incomplete_download}: \code{\link[=jatos_export_results]{jatos_export_results()}} when a component
result could not be downloaded.
\item \code{jatosr_file_exists}: a target file or batch folder is in the way and
\code{overwrite = FALSE}.
}

